<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sture family</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th–16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as House of Sture</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sture family was a Swedish noble family whose members governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> as regents during the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sten-sture-the-elder">Sten Sture the Elder</a> defeated the Danish king Christian I at Brunkeberg in 1471, and Svante Nilsson and Sten Sture the Younger continued to resist Danish kings until 1520. The family's leadership prepared the way for Swedish independence under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-i-of-sweden">Gustav Vasa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sture-family.jpg" alt="Sture family" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jürgen Howaldt · CC BY-SA 2.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stockholm-Storkyrkan_(St.Georg).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under the Kalmar Union, peasant armies led by Engelbrekt Engelbrektsson and the <b>Sture</b> regents resisted Danish kings, and Sten Sture the Elder defeated Christian I at the Battle of Brunkeberg in 1471.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sweden">Kingdom of Sweden · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Swedish regents of the <b>Sture family</b> often ruled in practice.</blockquote><a href="/state/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a></li></ul></section>
